# Deep Re-Audit & Bug Diagnosis Report

**Date:** 2026-02-17
**Scope:** All performance-related files (~2,800 lines across 16 files)
**Method:** Line-by-line code review with edge-case analysis

---

## Bug Severity Key

| Severity | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| 🔴 CRITICAL | Will cause incorrect behavior at runtime for a significant % of users |
| 🟠 HIGH | Causes incorrect behavior in specific edge cases or wastes significant resources |
| 🟡 MEDIUM | Suboptimal behavior, latent defect, or masked failure |
| ⚪ LOW | Code smell, missed optimization, or defensive coding gap |

---

## Bug Inventory

### 🔴 BUG-01: [classifyNetworkTier](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#124-146) — 3G Networks Classified as MINIMAL Instead of CONSTRAINED

**File:** [perfHints.ts L131-133](file:///wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#L131-L133)

```typescript
if (values.effectiveType === "slow-2g" || values.effectiveType === "2g" || values.effectiveType === "3g") {
  return "MINIMAL";  // ← BUG: 3G is NOT the same severity as 2G
}
```

**Root cause:** 3G is lumped with `slow-2g` and `2g`, all returning `"MINIMAL"`.

**Actual behavior:** A user on 3G (which can do 1-14 Mbps, 100-500ms RTT) gets the same MINIMAL treatment as a user on 2G (which is ~0.1 Mbps). This means:
- Poll interval: 6,000ms minimum (3× base)
- Prefetch: **completely disabled** (count=0, mode=none)
- WS reconnect delay: 2× base, clamped 1500-6000ms
- Retry count: 3

**Expected behavior:** 3G should return `"CONSTRAINED"` (poll 4000ms, prefetch 3 sequential with 5s delay, retry 3). `slow-2g` and `2g` should remain `"MINIMAL"`.

**Impact:** Millions of users globally on 3G networks get an overly degraded experience — no prefetching at all and 6s poll minimums when their network could handle 4s polls and 3 prefetch chunks.

**Fix:**
```diff
-if (values.effectiveType === "slow-2g" || values.effectiveType === "2g" || values.effectiveType === "3g") {
-  return "MINIMAL";
+if (values.effectiveType === "slow-2g" || values.effectiveType === "2g") {
+  return "MINIMAL";
+}
+if (values.effectiveType === "3g") {
+  return "CONSTRAINED";
 }
```

