### 🔴 BUG-02: [cacheIndexAndAssets](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/sw.ts#76-94) — Response Body Consumed Before Cache Put

**File:** [sw.ts L76-93](file:///wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/sw.ts#L76-L93)

```typescript
async function cacheIndexAndAssets(cache: Cache): Promise<void> {
  const htmlResponse = await fetch("/index.html", { cache: "no-store" }).catch(() => null);
  // ...
  await cache.put("/index.html", htmlResponse.clone());  // L81: clones and caches ✅

  const html = await htmlResponse.text();  // L83: consumes the ORIGINAL body ⚠️
  // ...
  // htmlResponse body is now consumed; but that's OK because we already cloned above.
}
```

**Assessment:** On closer review this is actually **not a bug** — `clone()` is called on L81 before [text()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/hooks/use-auth.tsx#59-71) on L83, and only the clone is put in cache while the original is consumed by [text()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/hooks/use-auth.tsx#59-71). This pattern is correct. **False positive.**

