### 🔴 BUG-03: `use-websocket` — [computeWsReconnectDelayMs](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#545-562) Called Without Current Hints

**File:** [use-websocket.tsx L114](file:///wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/hooks/use-websocket.tsx#L114)

```typescript
const nextAttemptDelay = computeWsReconnectDelayMs(attemptsSoFar, reconnectInterval);
```

**Root cause:** [computeWsReconnectDelayMs](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#545-562) has 3 parameters: [(attempt, baseMs, hints?)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/secureCache.ts#239-276). When [hints](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#209-224) is omitted, the function calls [getPerfHints()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#278-282) which always creates a fresh snapshot. This works correctly.

**But:** The `reconnectInterval` value captured in the [connect](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#523-526) closure (L133 deps) is the value from the **initial render** of [LiveUpdatesProvider](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/live/LiveUpdatesProvider.tsx#21-64). When [usePerfHints()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#283-286) re-evaluates and [wsReconnectBaseDelayMs()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#527-544) returns a new base delay, the `reconnectInterval` prop changes, causing [connect](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#523-526) to be rebuilt. However, any **active** [onclose](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/hooks/use-websocket.tsx#100-124) handler still holds the **old** [connect](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#523-526) closure — the old `reconnectInterval` is used for the in-flight reconnect attempt.

**Impact:** If network conditions change mid-reconnect-cycle (e.g., user switches from WiFi to 4G), the reconnect delay calculation uses the stale initial interval, not the updated one. The delay is recalculated using old `reconnectInterval` values.

**Severity reclassified:** 🟠 HIGH — Only triggers during active reconnection when network tier also changes simultaneously. Uncommon but real.

