### 🟠 BUG-04: [classifyDeviceTier](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#147-162) — Unreachable Line 160

**File:** [perfHints.ts L147-161](file:///wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#L147-L161)

```typescript
function classifyDeviceTier(values) {
  const memory = values.deviceMemoryGB;
  const cores = values.hardwareConcurrency;

  if (memory == null && cores == null) return "FAST";              // L154
  if ((memory != null && memory < 2) || (cores != null && cores < 2)) return "MINIMAL";  // L155
  if ((memory == null || memory >= 8) && (cores == null || cores >= 8)) return "INSTANT"; // L156
  if ((memory == null || memory >= 4) && (cores == null || cores >= 4)) return "FAST";    // L157
  if ((cores != null && cores >= 4) && (memory != null && memory >= 2)) return "MODERATE"; // L158
  if ((memory != null && memory >= 2) || (cores != null && cores >= 2)) return "CONSTRAINED"; // L159
  return "MODERATE";  // L160 — UNREACHABLE
}
```

**Proof:** After L154 excludes [(null, null)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/secureCache.ts#239-276), and L155 excludes `<2`, all remaining values have at least one non-null metric ≥2. L159 catches `memory >= 2 || cores >= 2`, which covers all remaining cases. L160 is dead code.

**Impact:** Not a runtime bug, but misleading — the fallback `"MODERATE"` is never returned.

