### 🟠 BUG-05: [refreshPerfHints](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#254-264) — Always Replaces Snapshot Even When Equal

**File:** [perfHints.ts L254-263](file:///wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#L254-L263)

```typescript
export function refreshPerfHints(): PerfHints {
  const next = createPerfHints();
  if (!hintsAreEqual(next, perfHintsSnapshot)) {
    perfHintsSnapshot = next;      // different → replace + notify ✅
    notifyPerfHintListeners();
  } else {
    perfHintsSnapshot = next;      // same → still replace ⚠️
  }
  return perfHintsSnapshot;
}
```

**Root cause:** The `else` branch replaces the snapshot reference even though values are equal. This means `useSyncExternalStore` sees a new object identity on every call to [getPerfHints()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#278-282).

**Impact:** [getPerfHints()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#278-282) is called from:
- [queryClient.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/queryClient.ts) L148: inside [retry()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/queryClient.ts#146-150) — called on every failed query retry
- [queryPersistence.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/queryPersistence.ts) L154: inside [getQueryPersistHydrateTimeoutMs()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/queryPersistence.ts#152-159)
- [recommendedPollIntervalMs()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#563-569) default param

Every call creates a new object. **However**, `useSyncExternalStore` uses the [getHintsSnapshot](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#273-277) function (L273-276) which returns the current `perfHintsSnapshot`. If [getPerfHints()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#278-282) is not called from within React render (which it isn't — it's only used outside of hooks), the snapshot replacement doesn't trigger extra renders. But it does create unnecessary garbage.

**Fix:**
```diff
  } else {
-   perfHintsSnapshot = next;
+   // No change — keep existing reference.
  }
```

